	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Type "emoji", or press Ctrl+Cmd+Space, then start typing to search by name (e.g. "smile", "fire"). Results are plain text (the actual emoji glyph, rendered natively) rather than generated images, so there's no icon rendering/decoding overhead on open.

Press Return to copy the selected emoji to the clipboard and paste it into the frontmost app. Press Cmd+Return to copy it without pasting.

Each item has a stable uid (the emoji itself), so Alfred's own usage-learning reorders results toward what you actually pick over time — no custom tracking needed.

Ctrl+Cmd+Space is also macOS's default "Emoji &amp; Symbols" shortcut. If it doesn't trigger this workflow, open Alfred's hotkey field for this workflow and re-press the combo, and/or free it up in System Settings &gt; Keyboard &gt; Keyboard Shortcuts.

The first time you use paste, macOS will ask you to grant Alfred Accessibility permission so it can simulate the paste keystroke — grant it in System Settings &gt; Privacy &amp; Security.

Emoji names/keywords from the gemoji project (github/gemoji, MIT licensed).</string>
